Publication Title	A CRISPR screen identifies UFMylation and TRAMP-like complexes required for hepatitis A virus infection
Publication Status	submitted
Publication Status Term Source REF
Publication Status Term Accession Number

Experiment Description	A knockout cell library in Huh7.5.1 cells was generated by introducing a genome-scale CRISPR library (GeCKOv2, Addgene #1000000049) and subjected to hepatitis A virus infection (HM175/18f) to isolate virus-resistant mutant cells. Genomic DNA was isolated from the original and virus-selected mutant cell populations and abundance of guideRNA encoding sequences were measured by sequencing on an Illumina NextSeq (High Output).

Protocol Name	P-MTAB-92495	P-MTAB-92494	P-MTAB-92493	P-MTAB-92492
Protocol Type	nucleic acid sequencing protocol	nucleic acid library construction protocol	nucleic acid extraction protocol	sample collection protocol
Protocol Term Source REF	EFO	EFO	EFO	EFO
Protocol Term Accession Number	EFO_0004170	EFO_0004184	EFO_0002944	EFO_0005518
Protocol Description	Libraries for the different samples were pooled and sequenced on an Illumina NextSeq (High Output).	Guide RNA encoding DNA sequences were amplified in a two-step nested PCR using KAPA HiFi HotStart ReadyMixPCR Kit (Kapa Biosystems).	Genomic DNA from control and virus-selected cell populations were extracted using QIAamp DNA Blood Maxi Kit (Qiagen).	A total of 60 million mutagenized cells for each sublibrary (A and B) were collected for genomic DNA extraction 10 days post-transduction with CRISPR libraries and used as control. A total of 45 million mutagenized cells for each sublibrary were infected with hepatitis A virus for 12 days and surviving cells were collected.
